# CrossEngin domain pack: physics fundamentals (v1)
#
# ~50 atoms + ~45 implications covering classical mechanics, gravity,
# electromagnetism, thermodynamics, and quantum-mechanics ontology at
# textbook granularity. Deliberate label overlap with solar_system
# (sun, star, planet, gravity, mass, atmosphere) so a cross-KG
# consistency scan compares both packs against each other.
#
# Ontological is-a edges get FORMAL strength (a force IS a
# physical_quantity; that's not up for Bayesian debate). Constitutive
# claims ("gravity attracts") stay EMPIRICAL so future evidence can
# refine belief.
#
# Ingest via:
#   /ingest cerec data/packs/physics.cerec physics src:pack:physics:v1
#
# After ingest (with solar_system + folk_astronomy also loaded):
#   /kg_consistency 200
# should surface labels present in multiple KGs with divergent beliefs.

KG physics
SRC src:pack:physics:v1

# ============================================================================
# 1. Root ontology: physical_quantity, force, particle, wave
# ============================================================================

ATOM physical_quantity 3 950
ATOM force 3 950
ATOM particle 3 950
ATOM wave 3 950
ATOM field 3 950
ATOM energy 3 950
ATOM mass 3 950

IMP force physical_quantity FORMAL
IMP energy physical_quantity FORMAL
IMP mass physical_quantity FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 2. The four fundamental forces
# ============================================================================

ATOM gravity 3 950
ATOM electromagnetism 3 950
ATOM weak_force 3 900
ATOM strong_force 3 900

IMP gravity force FORMAL
IMP electromagnetism force FORMAL
IMP weak_force force FORMAL
IMP strong_force force FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 3. Classical particles + basic taxonomy
# ============================================================================

ATOM electron 1 1000
ATOM proton 1 1000
ATOM neutron 1 1000
ATOM photon 1 1000
ATOM quark 1 950
ATOM neutrino 1 950
ATOM lepton 3 900
ATOM hadron 3 900
ATOM boson 3 900
ATOM fermion 3 900

IMP electron particle FORMAL
IMP proton particle FORMAL
IMP neutron particle FORMAL
IMP photon particle FORMAL
IMP quark particle FORMAL

IMP electron lepton FORMAL
IMP neutrino lepton FORMAL
IMP proton hadron FORMAL
IMP neutron hadron FORMAL
IMP photon boson FORMAL
IMP electron fermion FORMAL
IMP proton fermion FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 4. Celestial physics -- SHARED labels with solar_system
# ============================================================================
# These atoms use the SAME labels as data/packs/solar_system.cerec, but
# viewed from physics's angle (gravity, mass, luminosity, orbital
# mechanics). Both packs SHOULD agree on the high-confidence claims;
# any disagreement is a real thing worth surfacing.

ATOM star 3 1000
ATOM planet 3 1000
ATOM sun 1 1000
ATOM earth 1 1000
ATOM jupiter 1 1000

IMP star celestial_body FORMAL
ATOM celestial_body 3 950
IMP planet celestial_body FORMAL

# Physics-view: a star fuses hydrogen and emits radiation.
ATOM hydrogen_fusion 3 900
ATOM radiation 3 900
IMP star hydrogen_fusion EMPIRICAL
IMP sun hydrogen_fusion EMPIRICAL
IMP hydrogen_fusion radiation EMPIRICAL
IMP star radiation EMPIRICAL

# Gravity is the dominant force between celestial bodies.
IMP celestial_body gravity EMPIRICAL
IMP earth gravity EMPIRICAL
IMP sun gravity EMPIRICAL
IMP jupiter gravity EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 5. Thermodynamics + statistical mechanics
# ============================================================================

ATOM temperature 3 950
ATOM entropy 3 950
ATOM heat 3 900
ATOM second_law_thermodynamics 3 950

IMP temperature physical_quantity FORMAL
IMP entropy physical_quantity FORMAL
IMP heat energy EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 6. Waves / light / electromagnetism
# ============================================================================

ATOM light 3 950
ATOM electromagnetic_wave 3 950
IMP light electromagnetic_wave FORMAL
IMP electromagnetic_wave wave FORMAL
IMP photon light EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 7. Cross-source citations
# ============================================================================

CITE src:pack:physics:v1 src:paper:doi:standard-model-of-particle-physics supports
CITE src:pack:physics:v1 src:paper:doi:einstein-general-relativity-1915 extends
CITE src:pack:physics:v1 src:pack:solar_system:v1 supports

# ============================================================================
# 8. Observations reinforcing highest-confidence claims
# ============================================================================

OBS gravity +1 1000
OBS electron +1 1000
OBS photon +1 1000
